title: 'sp-api: Use EncodeLike for runtime API client-side parameters'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Runtime API client-side methods generated by `decl_runtime_apis!` now accept any argument that
    SCALE-encodes like the declared parameter type, via `parity_scale_codec::EncodeLike`: each
    parameter is generic over `EncodeLike<DeclaredType>`, so a value or a reference to it can be
    passed at no runtime cost. Parameterised methods gain a `where Self: Sized` bound to stay
    dyn-compatible, and `mock_impl_runtime_apis!` decodes the generic arguments back to the declared
    types internally.

    Since `EncodeLike` is not implemented for every encodable type by default, the block component
    traits used as runtime API parameters now require the `EncodeLike` marker:
    `sp_runtime::traits::{Header, LazyBlock}`, `Block::Extrinsic` and
    `sp_consensus_beefy::AuthorityIdBound`. Every `Encode`-deriving type already satisfies this, so
    no implementor changes are needed. A few node-side call sites that relied on inference (bare
    `vec![]` / `None`) now need explicit types.

crates:
# Crates whose generated runtime API traits or public bounds changed. The new generic
# parameters and `EncodeLike` marker bounds are satisfied by every type that already derives
# `Encode`, so no implementor changes are required; hence `validate: false`.
- name: sp-api
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: sp-api-proc-macro
  bump: patch
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: sp-consensus-beefy
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: sp-block-builder
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: sp-session
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: mmr-rpc
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: substrate-frame-rpc-system
  bump: major
  validate: false
# Crates that only adjusted internal call sites to the runtime APIs.
- name: sc-service
  bump: none
- name: sc-rpc
  bump: none
- name: sc-transaction-pool
  bump: none
- name: sc-basic-authorship
  bump: none
- name: sc-tracing
  bump: none
- name: frame-benchmarking-cli
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-client-service
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: none
